  "description": "Fired tubular reactor in which natural gas or another light hydrocarbon reacts with steam over a nickel catalyst to make synthesis gas, followed in ammonia plants by a secondary reformer where air or oxygen is added and the remaining methane is converted. Reformers set the hydrogen-to-nitrogen ratio and the methane slip for the downstream shift and synthesis sections. Primary source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam_reforming",
  "applications": [
    "hydrogen and ammonia synthesis gas production",
    "methanol and refinery hydrogen plants"
  ],
